A||||32||FieroLisa||Why People Make Me Mad...||||1||
Z||000000||FieroLisa||07-10-2001||08:04 PM||||So I haven't posted in a while, but since I'm off work early, for a reason I'll describe later, I figure I could use this time to b*tch and moan.<P>Here's my situation.<P>I work for a company, and my dad is CEO of this company... my dad and I live in 2 different states, but the people that work there treat me freakin funny since they are scared of me or something, either that or just think I'm gonna be a b*tch.<P>So I work at one of the stores here in Greensboro and I do a freakin good job... Right now my sales are about twice of what the stores *top* sales rep is at... (and when you get commission that's good for the Fiero spending account!) Anyway and I get along with everyone at this store, which is good since they are understaffed. Another store across town is overstaffed, and anyway I don't know the people there well and feel generally uncomfortable around them...the store is tiny, they have too many people... I got one sale when I worked there today when I normally get between 5 and 8 at my normal store. <P>SO! About a half hour away there is another store.. (haha there are lots) where I'm friends with this guy. JUST friends! BUT everyone there is just talkin this whole thing up... too bad this guy is *MARRIED* with a kid (OK so he's only 21)  First of all, what am I going to do with a married guy, and why must people talk sh*t?  Now, granted I am good friends with this guy, hell he is basically the only good friend I have in this area, so we talk like every day... <P>SO anyway NOW my stupid manager's boss has decided that I shouldn't work at my normal store...for some *unknown* reason. I know it has to do with these rumors since my boss is my friends brother. So they moved me to this overstaffed crap @ss store where I can't sell anything. No one at that store knows why I'm there, since they have 3 extra sales reps.    <P>so WHAT THE H*LL?? ARG.<P>So I'm wondering if these rumors got to my manager's boss and without asking me, is trying to do something about it? Anyway my sales are going to go way down working at this other store I think, and I just don't like working there!!!<P>WORK SUCKS. <P>K I'm done b*tching now, as I'm sure none of the above makes much sense by now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jaygee79||07-10-2001||08:35 PM||||<FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="purple">Wow, that sucks.  Can you try to talk to the mamager from the normal store and find out why you got moved?  Maybe there's another reason (probably not, but maybe).If that doesn't work you could go higher up and ask to be transferred back to your normal store.  Kinda stupid that they have that many extra people, why would they add to it?  Anyway, good luck.</FONT></FONT><P>------------------<BR>Jaime<BR>84SE red<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooh14.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||07-10-2001||08:55 PM||||Jaime: I talked to my manager from my normal store this morning... he was arguing with the supervisor to keep me at his store, since my sales have been so good.<P>I did talk to a "higher-up", my dad- but I didn't expect him to snap his fingers and make something happen, but I did ask him for advice as to what I should do in the situation. He gave me some, and I took it, which was to email the supervisor as to why I got moved...of course he gave me some lame reason.<P>And what almost p*sses me off the worst is that people will NOT quit with these rumors... I don't even know how to begin to tell them to shut up!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||07-10-2001||08:59 PM||||Lisa, Welcome to the world of office politics.<P>I can't say too much except the CEO's daughter is friends with an oppisite sex married employee.  No one in the store will believe that, even when it is true. You will have to walk a tight line to make sure there is no appearence of anything happening.<P>There must be a zone manager who understands staffing level needs and sales per store to determine who needs to go where.  If the overstaffed poor sales store is a problem of location, maybe the store needs to be evaluated and shut down.<P>If you can use your charms and skills as a sales person, maybe you can boost your sales in that store and show them how it is done.<P>Sales is a tough business with various employee personalities.  However this is, at this time, a summer job for you'll go back to school shortly.<P>This is a learning experience for you, the rest of the staff may be thinking the CEO's daughter will be in charge shortly and be nice to her.  Your boss may be looking out for his brother's career.  Lets see a fling with the CEO's daughter which doesn't work out... he's out the door.  It's all appearences.  <P>I'd say cool it on the daily conversations, and what you'd do with a married guy with child, would be the same thing as with a single guy, but with more strings to get entangled and more consequences.<P>Hopefully this will all get fixed by Williamsburg time.  I'd buy you a drink at the Ramada, but are you of legal age?||||reg||1
Z||000004||RoadRocket||07-10-2001||09:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>And what almost p*sses me off the worst is that people will NOT quit with these rumors... I don't even know how to begin to tell them to shut up!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Welcome to the wonderful world of politics, FieroLisa.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> It ain't just for politicians.<P>It doesn't matter what you do, how careful you are about how you do it, or even what you intended when you did it. Someone, somewhere will always find something wrong with it. <P>It's just human nature.<P>Probably the only thing you can do about your transfer is enlist your manager to help get you back. <P>Or you can ask your father for help, but that will create a different set of rumors.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>There is little you can do about the rumors, short of ending your friendship with your married friend. You can try and control the rumors, but people will think what they want to think. <P>I know that ain't much help. It's just a sad fact of life that you sometimes have to learn to live with.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||07-10-2001||09:44 PM||||Thats a shame about your situation, but thats the human condition.  Its one thing for people to talk poo at work, but it sucks when it hits you where it hurts...the wallet (or purse in your case).   <P>If they keep it up even now that youve been uprooted, just tell them to grow up.  It probably wont do any good, but it might make you feel better.  Ultimately though, the best way to get back at those people is to maintain a good attitude and never let them see that what they did bothers you.  That usually pisses people off worse than anything else.  <P>Keep your head up.  Things have a way of working themselves out.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
