Z||000019||FieroLisa||07-12-2001||11:30 AM||||Roger and Ken, now you guys both hush!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I don't like my 2 future husbands to argue.<P>Anyway back to the original subject. I knew I couldn't ask my dad to snap his fingers and make something happen, thats no way to gain respect, which is what I have been working for here.  Buuuut I have asked him for advice, and he's given it to me.  The regional manager wrote me an email and blatantly lied to me about why he moved me... so at my Dad's advice, I'm writing him an email essentially saying (but written profesionally of course) " I just want to confirm you're relocating me for such and such reason. The reason i ask is because I know there are some rumors and I want to make sure those have nothing to do with your decision. I want to work where it is best for the company, so if your decision is based on the rumors, I would like to discuss things with you since, as most rumors do, I'm sure they have been exaggerated by each person telling them."<P><BR>And now I'm off to go fix my car so I can get my butt to the Michigan show!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000020||rogergarrison||07-12-2001||11:35 AM||||lisa, if you see this before you call. Your Fiero Drag Racing magazine is here.||||reg||1
Z||000021||Patrick's Dad||07-12-2001||12:31 PM||||<BR>From FieroLisa: " And now I'm off to go fix my car so I can get my butt to the Michigan show!!!!!!"<P>...maybe the rest of you, too. Sorry, couldn't resist.<P>Having been in retail almost all of your life, I understand your feelings about being moved around, especially to a slower store. Maybe you can turn this into an opportunity, as in selling the heck out of the place, and showing the others how it's done. In this, you vindicate yourself as a professional who can get the job done, not as "Daddy's Girl." That way, when you're out of school, and you're an exec of the company, you can fire all the idiots.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I was moved from a store location that I had opened and was growing to the "former" #4 (of 4) store. Sales rose 12% for the year, and 35% in the last quarter (compared with the previous year) with some careful staffing improvements. My store (I was the manager) became #3, and for the holiday season, was the #2 location.<P>People are people. I have a customer now who wants to be my assistant for a photo shoot that I'm doing for a friend of mine. My wife didn't like this, as this customer is a she. A single she. My wife and I came to terms with this, but, a previous poster is right. You can do anything with a married man that you can do with a single one. Just don't, and, in the end, all that matters is that you and he know that you were right. Hey, I worked for a bank for a short time, and I got fired (not officially) for dating a teller. The bank is faltering, and the teller and I have two beautiful kids. It all works out in the end.||||reg||1
Z||000022||artherd||07-13-2001||06:09 AM||||If I had a Star like Lisa working for me, I would put her in the slowest store to show those overstaffed, under-achieving louts how it was done :)<P>Oh, on the roumours, you can always pull a Milton from Office Space.....<P>Or just whenever anyone asks "hey, so are you and so-and-so, you-know?" just respond in the outrageously affirmative (Ie, yes, infact we are getting hitched and moving to Kosovo).  It ceases to be funny real fast if it NO LONGER annoys you... (people are dumb. Especially when they nave nothing better to do.)<P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000023||Justin||07-13-2001||11:26 AM||||Here is what I would do:<P>I would do whatever it takes to make me happy.  If that means talking to a friend, so be it.  I would not stop taking to someone just because people make up rumors.  I wouldn't give a crap what anyone says about me.  Everyone has there own opinions, some people just don't know how to shut up about it.  I wouldn't get back at them, just ignore them.  Then I would do everything in my power to get put back where I want to be.  If this means stop talking to that person, then I would weigh out which is more important.  But I would not stop talking to someone just because of other people who are rude enough and that screwed up in the head that they ned to sink to the fouth grade level to spread rumors, like too many of todays people already do.  I would just do what I want as long as it does not cause harm to anyone else and I know what I am doing is the right thing in my head.  But this is just what I would do.  Take it how you want.<P>But for you, I would suggest figuring out what is more important for you, in the long run.  Is this person going to be there for you and be a friend in the years to come?  Are you going to have a good job that you like at your current business in the future?  Think of the long run.  If you can deal with whatever streses are holding you down for a little while longer, maybe everything will work out OK after this has blown by.  I really cannot see a rumor like this lasting more then a few weeks, maybe 2 months at the most.  Unless of course it really does end up a twisted mess, and you get in trouble somehow.  Just do what you need to do, and what you think is right, and everything will be OK.  That's all I got for ya.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>If at first you don't succeed, pretend you were never trying in the first place.<P>visit <A HREF="http://www.twinkiesproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.twinkiesproject.com</A>  for information on the chemical properties, reactions, gravitational resonse, and density issues of a Twinkie.||||reg||1
Z||000024||rogergarrison||07-13-2001||12:56 PM||||youll be coming back to school in a month or so........just blow it off.||||reg||1
Z||000025||EdsB52||07-13-2001||12:57 PM||||Lisa, this is very simple. Just ask the manager out for a platonic dinner in celebration of your acceptance of your position at the new store. Once you're seated, have your dad show up and join the two of you, either by surprise acquaintance or design (which ever works best for the given situation). Then introduce your dad to this manager in a subtle, but direct fashion. Underlying messages have far more leveraging ability than overt, blatant threats because they're open-ended.<P>Toss this idea around and see if it will work for you. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000026||deluxe827||07-14-2001||11:52 PM||||Well lisa...  The hole thing will blow over,  dont use your dad.  You are correct  if you handle it your self then people might respect you for you, not the "CEO's daughter" .   Call Chuck what a jackass wow talk about self respect when you make a comment like that.  As far as the married guy dont let people break a great friendship over rumor's.  You seem to be smart , just let everthing take its course and it will all work out for the best(you know what I mean).  Anywho take care  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||12
Z||000027||EdsB52||07-15-2001||04:20 AM||||What "hole thing?" My opinion stands that you should use your dad with subtle discretion. Without his persuasion you've lost money and opportunity and may lose more. Fail to use that device and maintain your dignity (as prescribed by people who fail); use him and gain respect. Fear is a component of respect; respect is a component of fear. Who cares, the manager drew first blood through the misuse of his authority which was ultimately given by your dad. Your dad could vicariously restore your opportunity through careful persuasion. Your choice; live with an abstract form of dignity or be a success.||||reg||1
Z||000028||FieroLisa||07-15-2001||05:53 PM||||Well this "whole situation" has seemed to calm down... luckily. I've been gone for 5 days, so hopefully things will stay calm when I get back. I'm gonna feel really bad for this guy if sh*t starts up again.<P>I think deluxe827 is exactly right in not using my dad.... I've tried not to bring anything up, act any different or get any special treatment. This same situation might happen at any later job I have, no matter who I am related too...<P>Now I just need to get back to working in my normal store so I can make money to pay off that dang Michigan show!!!!! (And the speeding ticket I got on the way down there)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000029||87GTZ34||07-15-2001||08:32 PM||||Lisa,  If you want to stop rumors like those dead in their tracks, have your friend have his wife & child stop over for lunch (or a break) and then all four of you can show the busy bodies that they're wasting air.  Of course the rumors could turn to cheap talk of threesomes and whatnot... GL||||reg||1
Z||000030||deluxe827||07-15-2001||10:21 PM||||Well Good...  I am glad to see everything has calmed down for you...  As far as the married guy goes, watch yourself they can be frisky  lol   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  as always take care<P>||||reg||1
Z||000031||fierohoho||07-16-2001||02:32 PM||||Problems:<P>#1- People are intimidated by an intelligent and articulate woman.<P>#2- People who have no lives will gosip, whether its true or false to put some sort of excitement or meaning into their pitiful lives.<P>Solution:<P>#1- Blacken out several teeth, mis-spell things like "hambirger", talk like you have an IQ of 12. People will then leave you alone.<P>#2- Have your dad put out a memo to all employees advising them they have 30 days to: buy a Fiero, buy a computer, join a Fiero club and log-on to Pennock's. With these items they will now have a life.<P>Otherwise just say F***it, Be yourself and let em stew. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000032||Slammed Fiero||07-17-2001||10:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by deluxe827:<BR><B>Well lisa...  The hole thing will blow over,  dont use your dad.  You are correct  if you handle it your self then people might respect you for you, not the "CEO's daughter" .   Call Chuck what a jackass wow talk about self respect when you make a comment like that.  As far as the married guy dont let people break a great friendship over rumor's.  You seem to be smart , just let everthing take its course and it will all work out for the best(you know what I mean).  Anywho take care   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Ahh it was a joke there buddy ,I know Lisa pretty well , probably better than 99.9% of the forum members, So I'm allowed to make little inside jokes. Simmer down.<P>JM <P>||||reg||1
